silm:instances_papers_16_one_integrated_growing_knowledge_graph_chapters_02_cross_entity_reference_arrows_sections_03_sees_as_patient_yoneda_hom_legs a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "SeesAsPatientYonedaHomLegsExample" .
silm:instances_papers_16_one_integrated_growing_knowledge_graph_chapters_02_cross_entity_reference_arrows_sections_03_sees_as_patient_yoneda_hom_legs silm:hasExample "In 'SeesAsPatientYonedaHomLegs', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, sees_as_patient (Vet -> Mittens) : Vet77_apex -> colim D_Mittens; Dr. Patel sees Mittens as a patient; the role arrow is typed, NOT the identity (the vet is not the cat).; also, sees_as_patient (Vet -> Pumpkin) : Vet77_apex -> colim D_Pumpkin; Dr. Patel also sees Pumpkin as a patient; two distinct role arrows from one vet to two patients preserve both as distinct sub-apices." .
